      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Available** = resources Kubernetes allows pods to use, after system reservations. It is not unused capacity. **Requested** = reported workload requests. **Limit (reported)** = sum of the limits received; some containers may have no limit. **Used** = latest reported usage. CPU is in cores; memory uses KiB/MiB/GiB automatically.\n\n**Current data issue:** recent request records lack cluster names. Node tables do not require that label. Cluster tables include labeled records only and may be incomplete; namespace tables need one exact cluster name below. UNLABELED records remain visible in the checks below, not combined into a fictitious cluster. Total physical CPU/RAM capacity is not collected in the supplied samples.\n\nDefault window: **last 2 minutes**. This is a recent-sample view, not a guaranteed live Kubernetes inventory. Confirm collector interval before use."
